    },
    "message": "feat(updates): show release notes in the update banner\n\nThe banner announced a version number and linked out. A number alone does not\ntell an operator whether an update matters to them, so the interesting part of\na release -- what actually changed -- was one click away and usually unread.\n\nThe release feed already returns the notes; they were simply never read.\nReleaseStatus now carries release_notes from the payload body, and the banner\nrenders them in a collapsed \"What changed\" section.\n\nBounded at 4000 characters with a trailing ellipsis: the feed is remote, so the\nbanner shows an excerpt and keeps the existing link for the rest rather than\nrendering an unbounded blob into the dashboard.\n\nVerification: tests cover the notes reaching ReleaseStatus and as_dict, a blank\nbody yielding None, and the length bound. Exercised against the live feed --\ndetects 4.20.0 from 4.18.2 and pulls the title plus trimmed notes. Full suite\npasses except 14 failures that also fail on unmodified main (8 from real API\nkeys in the local environment, 6 PowerShell installer tests).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
